WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.524
The results are decisive.

00:00:01.604 --> 00:00:03.192
On synthetic block models,

00:00:03.272 --> 00:00:10.185
the test using cumulants achieves a consistently
higher area under the ROC curve than the test using moments,

00:00:10.265 --> 00:00:14.548
and the advantage widens as the number of graphs
per sample shrinks.

00:00:14.628 --> 00:00:18.783
The moment test breaks down entirely below four
graphs per sample,

00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:21.798
where its covariance estimate becomes singular,

00:00:21.878 --> 00:00:26.482
while the cumulant test keeps working all the way
down to a single graph.

00:00:26.562 --> 00:00:31.678
The same pattern holds on real biological networks:
with edge density held equal,

00:00:31.758 --> 00:00:35.785
adding more subgraph orders steadily sharpens the
cumulant test,

00:00:35.865 --> 00:00:39.570
whereas it makes the moment test overfit and
perform worse.
